# Little Browser (Android): the little window (docs/ux.md §8, §10). A web link from another app
# opens in a Custom Tab of its own rather than as a tab (app.littlebrowser.lb.shell.LittleWindow
# decides and marks it); the browser's own launches, a site's home-screen shortcut among them,
# don't. That Custom Tab's toolbar has Copy URL and "Open in ‹space›", which moves the page into
# the browser's window through Custom Tabs' "open in browser" reparenting, without reloading it,
# whichever browser is the device's default, and into the window of the page's profile (the
# default one, a Custom Tab's): that window while it is open, else that window again; not
# whichever window was in front. The toolbar's buttons come from
# CustomTabToolbarButtonsCoordinator's model, which gets a way to add one.

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/document/ChromeLauncherActivity.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/document/ChromeLauncherActivity.java
